WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.187
Choosing an AI video tool comes down to one question: what do you need it to

2
00:00:06.187 --> 00:00:06.838
produce?

3
00:00:06.838 --> 00:00:11.099
A footage generator creates new moving images from a prompt.

4
00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.058
A presenter tool delivers a script on screen with an avatar.

5
00:00:15.058 --> 00:00:21.799
A source-to-video workflow turns a webpage, article or data record into a finished

6
00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:22.210
clip.

7
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.982
A programmatic system applies the same template to many changing records.

8
00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:32.209
Some products combine several of these jobs, which is why category labels can

9
00:00:32.209 --> 00:00:32.752
mislead.

10
00:00:32.752 --> 00:00:39.941
Before comparing tools, write a clear brief: define your input, your required output

11
00:00:39.941 --> 00:00:42.423
and your acceptance criteria.

12
00:00:42.423 --> 00:00:46.753
Then give each candidate the same difficult test case.

13
00:00:46.753 --> 00:00:52.842
Count the total work, including review and corrections, not just the time until a

14
00:00:52.842 --> 00:00:54.045
render finishes.

15
00:00:54.045 --> 00:01:00.032
For teams producing video at scale, check whether brand controls, source accuracy

16
00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:03.506
and approval steps are built into the workflow.
